  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n2 (3)/(7) times[(11 (2)/(6) div((25)/(18)+2 (5)/(6)-(7)/(36)))]=y div 72.5 times 204\n\n**Concept Used:**\n\nBodmas\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nSimplifying the given expression gives\n\n2 (3)/(7) times[(11 (2)/(6) div((25)/(18)+2 (5)/(6)-(7)/(36)))]=y div 72.5 times 204\n\n(17)/(7) times[((68)/(6) div((25)/(18)+ (17)/(6)-(7)/(36)))]= (y)/(72.5)times 204\n\n(17)/(7) times[((68)/(6) div((50+102 -7)/(36)))]= (y)/(72.5)times 204\n\n(17)/(7) times[((68)/(6) times(36)/(145))]= (y)/(72.5)times 204\n\n(17)/(7) times[((408)/(145))]= (y)/(72.5)times 204\n\n(17)/(7) ×408= 408y\n\ny = 17/7\n\n**Hence, the value of y is 17/7.**",
